<item>
            <title>[ZEPPELIN-79] Zeppelin does not kill some interpreters when server is stopped</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-79</link>
                <project id="12316221" key="ZEPPELIN">Zeppelin</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;When the Zeppelin server is stopped (e.g., with a SIGTERM), it should also stop all interpreter processes that it has started.  Instead, I sometimes see them hang around as orphaned children after the Zeppelin server has stopped.  This seems to be the case with the spark interpreter (at least with yarn-client mode; haven&apos;t tested with standalone or local modes) and with the shell interpreter.  It does not seem to occur with the hive or angular interpreters; those ones stop when the server is stopped.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
        <key id="12829738">ZEPPELIN-79</key>
            <summary>Zeppelin does not kill some interpreters when server is stopped</summary>
